      "note": "Intentional customer-code execution boundary. ServiceExecutor runs an explicitly declared repository-contained Ruby entrypoint only in the executor. The executable is fixed to RbConfig.ruby, no shell is invoked, entrypoint realpath must stay inside the disposable customer checkout, and arguments are passed as argv. The control plane never executes customer code, executor deployments receive no GitHub App private key or webhook secret, and the repository read capability is not persisted. Production Lab and remote-executor topology prove these surrounding isolation boundaries. This suppresses only this exact Brakeman fingerprint, not the Execute check globally."
